  "result": "## Summary\n\nThe issue: `CliRunner` replaces `sys.stdout`/`sys.stderr` with wrappers backed by `io.BytesIO`. When code under test does something like `subprocess.run(..., stdout=sys.stderr)`, `subprocess` needs a real file descriptor (`stdout.fileno()`), but `io.BytesIO` doesn't support `fileno()`, raising `io.UnsupportedOperation`.\n\n**Fix** (in `src/click/testing.py`): `BytesIOCopy` (the class backing `StreamMixer.stdout`/`.stderr`) now lazily backs itself with a real on-disk `tempfile.TemporaryFile` the first time `fileno()` is called, mirroring both prior and subsequent writes into it. Normal usage (no `fileno()` call) is unaffected \u2014 no extra file descriptor is created, avoiding resource leaks. Added a proper `close()` override to clean up the lazily-created temp file, and `isolation()` now closes the stdout/stderr streams in its `finally` block after the captured values have already been read.\n\nVerified:\n- The reported reproduction case (`subprocess.run([\"echo\", \"foo\"], stdout=sys.stderr)` inside a `CliRunner`-invoked command) now passes.\n- Full existing test suite: `1419 passed, 24 skipped, 1 xfailed` \u2014 no regressions.",
